#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:91
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of SDDM"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:94
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"First, create a dedicated user and group to take control of the "
"<command>sddm</command> daemon after it is started. Issue the following "
"commands as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:100
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>groupadd -g 64 sddm &amp;&amp;\n"
"useradd  -c \"sddm Daemon\" \\\n"
"         -d /var/lib/sddm \\\n"
"         -u 64 -g sddm    \\\n"
"         -s /bin/false sddm</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:129
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>sddm</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:133
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr        \\\n"
"      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release         \\\n"
"      -D CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 \\\n"
"      -D ENABLE_JOURNALD=OFF              \\\n"
"      -D NO_SYSTEMD=ON                    \\\n"
"      -D RUNTIME_DIR=/run/sddm            \\\n"
"      -D USE_ELOGIND=ON                   \\\n"
"      -D BUILD_MAN_PAGES=ON               \\\n"
"      -D BUILD_WITH_QT6=ON                \\\n"
"      -D DATA_INSTALL_DIR=/usr/share/sddm \\\n"
"      -D DBUS_CONFIG_FILENAME=sddm_org.freedesktop.DisplayManager.conf \\\n"
"      .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:150
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr        \\\n"
"      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release         \\\n"
"      -D CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 \\\n"
"      -D RUNTIME_DIR=/run/sddm            \\\n"
"      -D BUILD_MAN_PAGES=ON               \\\n"
"      -D BUILD_WITH_QT6=ON                \\\n"
"      -D DATA_INSTALL_DIR=/usr/share/sddm \\\n"
"      -D DBUS_CONFIG_FILENAME=sddm_org.freedesktop.DisplayManager.conf \\\n"
"      .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:165
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:169
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:172
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make install &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -dm755 -o sddm -g sddm /var/lib/sddm\n"
"/usr/bin/sddm --example-config > /etc/sddm.conf</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:179
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:182
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release</parameter>: This switch is used to "
"apply additional compiler optimizations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:190
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D ENABLE_JOURNALD=OFF</parameter> and <parameter>-D "
"NO_SYSTEMD=ON</parameter>: These switches are used because this version of "
"BLFS does not support <application>systemd</application>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:196
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D "
"DBUS_CONFIG_FILENAME=sddm_org.freedesktop.DisplayManager.conf</parameter>: "
"This switch prevents the file <filename> "
"/etc/dbus-1/system.d/org.freedesktop.DisplayManager.conf</filename> from "
"being overwritten, as it may be used by other DM's."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:203
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D BUILD_MAN_PAGES=ON</parameter>: This switch is used to build "
"and install man pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:210
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring SDDM"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:213
#, xml-text
msgid "Config Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:216
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/sddm.config"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:220
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/sddm.conf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:224
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Normally, you want to edit this file. For example, if Xorg is installed in "
"/opt, use your preferred editor as the &root; user to replace the default "
"<emphasis>XauthPath</emphasis> value by "
"<emphasis>/opt/xorg/bin/xauth</emphasis>. Or, as the &root; user, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:231
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed -i.orig '/ServerPath/ s|usr|opt/xorg|' "
"/etc/sddm.conf</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:234
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This command will do the substitution and create a copy of the original file"
" with name <filename>/etc/sddm.conf.orig</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:239
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"From now on, we will describe how to modify configurations using sed.  Of "
"course, you may instead use your preferred editor as the &root; user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:245
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For security reasons, you normally want the default "
"<emphasis>ServerArguments=-nolisten tcp</emphasis>, unless a remote machine "
"needs access to the local X server. In that case, as the &root; user, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:251
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>sed -i 's/-nolisten tcp//' /etc/sddm.conf</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:254
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Desktop (Notebook) users, normally want the Num Lock key on (off).  For "
"that, as &root;, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:258
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>sed -i '/Numlock/s/none/on/' /etc/sddm.conf</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:261
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"for Desktop users. For Notebook users, replace /on/ by /off/ in the command "
"above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:266
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"By default, a virtual keyboard is presented for the user.  If this is not "
"desired, run as &root;:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:270
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>sed -i 's/qtvirtualkeyboard//' /etc/sddm.conf</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:275
#, xml-text
msgid "Boot Script"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:278
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install the <filename revision=\"sysv\">/etc/rc.d/init.d/xdm</filename> init"
" script from the <xref linkend=\"bootscripts\" revision=\"sysv\"/> package, "
"as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:284
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Enable the pre-installed systemd unit by running the following command as "
"the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:292
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install-sddm</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:294
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>systemctl enable sddm</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:299
#, xml-text
msgid "Linux PAM Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:303
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The install procedure above installed a set of PAM configuration files. "
"These procedures overwrite them and use versions compatible with a BLFS "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:310
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have built <application>sddm</application> with <application>Linux "
"PAM</application> support, create the necessary configuration files by "
"running the following commands as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:316
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/sddm &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/sddm\n"
"\n"
"auth     requisite      pam_nologin.so\n"
"auth     required       pam_env.so\n"
"\n"
"auth     required       pam_succeed_if.so uid &gt;= 1000 quiet\n"
"auth     include        system-auth\n"
"\n"
"account  include        system-account\n"
"password include        system-password\n"
"\n"
"session  required       pam_limits.so\n"
"session  include        system-session\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/sddm</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/sddm-autologin &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/sddm-autologin\n"
"\n"
"auth     requisite      pam_nologin.so\n"
"auth     required       pam_env.so\n"
"\n"
"auth     required       pam_succeed_if.so uid &gt;= 1000 quiet\n"
"auth     required       pam_permit.so\n"
"\n"
"account  include        system-account\n"
"\n"
"password required       pam_deny.so\n"
"\n"
"session  required       pam_limits.so\n"
"session  include        system-session\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/sddm-autologin</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/sddm-greeter &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/sddm-greeter\n"
"\n"
"auth     required       pam_env.so\n"
"auth     required       pam_permit.so\n"
"\n"
"account  required       pam_permit.so\n"
"password required       pam_deny.so\n"
"session  required       pam_unix.so\n"
"-session optional       pam_systemd.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/sddm-greeter</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:367
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/sddm &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/sddm\n"
"\n"
"auth     requisite      pam_nologin.so\n"
"auth     required       pam_env.so\n"
"\n"
"auth     required       pam_succeed_if.so uid &gt;= 1000 quiet\n"
"auth     include        system-auth\n"
"\n"
"account  include        system-account\n"
"password include        system-password\n"
"\n"
"session  required       pam_limits.so\n"
"session  include        system-session\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/sddm</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/sddm-autologin &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/sddm-autologin\n"
"\n"
"auth     requisite      pam_nologin.so\n"
"auth     required       pam_env.so\n"
"\n"
"auth     required       pam_succeed_if.so uid &gt;= 1000 quiet\n"
"auth     required       pam_permit.so\n"
"\n"
"account  include        system-account\n"
"\n"
"password required       pam_deny.so\n"
"\n"
"session  required       pam_limits.so\n"
"session  include        system-session\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/sddm-autologin</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/sddm-greeter &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/sddm-greeter\n"
"\n"
"auth     required       pam_env.so\n"
"auth     required       pam_permit.so\n"
"\n"
"account  required       pam_permit.so\n"
"password required       pam_deny.so\n"
"session  required       pam_unix.so\n"
"-session optional       pam_systemd.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/sddm-greeter</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:421
#, xml-text
msgid "Starting sddm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:424
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If the sddm bootscript has been installed, start sddm by running, as the "
"&root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:428
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>/etc/rc.d/init.d/xdm start</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:431
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"By convention, X should be executed at runlevel 5, consequently, the same is"
" true for <application>sddm</application>. However, the default runlevel is "
"3. Changing to runlevel 5, from a console terminal, as <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user, starts the "
"<command>sddm</command> bootscript, bringing up the greeter screen:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:438
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>init 5</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:441
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"In order to permanently set the default to 5, starting the "
"<command>sddm</command> greeter screen automatically, modify "
"<filename>/etc/inittab</filename> as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:447
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cp -v /etc/inittab{,-orig} &amp;&amp;\n"
"sed -i '/initdefault/ s/3/5/' /etc/inittab</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:453
#, xml-text
msgid "Available Sessions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:456
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The greeter offers a list of available sessions, depending on the Window "
"Managers and Desktop Environments installed. The list includes sessions "
"which have a corresponding <filename>.desktop</filename> file installed "
"under <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/share/xsessions</filename> or "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr/share/wayland-sessions</filename>.  Most "
"of the Window Managers and Desktop Environments automatically provide those "
"files, but if necessary, you may include a custom one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:469
#, xml-text
msgid "Themes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:472
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Three themes are installed at <filename class=\"directory\"> "
"/usr/share/sddm/themes</filename>: elarun, maldives, and maya.  There is "
"also a default theme, which is not present in that directory.  You can "
"install other themes in that directory. In order to change the theme, you "
"need to edit <filename>/etc/sddm.conf</filename>, to change the default "
"(empty) theme, replacing <literal>Current=</literal> with "
"<literal>Current=<replaceable>&lt;new theme&gt;</replaceable></literal>, "
"e.g. <literal>Current=maldives</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:487
#, xml-text
msgid "In order to see the theme without leaving the session, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/dm/sddm.xml:490
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sddm-greeter --test-mode --theme <replaceable>&lt;theme "
"path&gt;</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

